.TH CSTRING_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_reset \- clear all characters and shrink capacity to minimum
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

void cstring_reset(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Sets the length to zero and attempts to shrink the buffer back to the
minimum capacity (16 bytes). If the reallocation to shrink fails the
capacity is left unchanged; the length is always reset to zero regardless.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to reset
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_set (3),
.BR cstring_is_empty (3)
